e size of any clinical population. The molecular-confirmation stage behind those denominators (26/58/12/67) is a DIFFERENT set of integers from the named-partner counts (24/57/11/62). WITHDRAWN 2026-09-08, and this entry previously asserted all of them: the two-cohort 73-patient pooled prognostic magnitude (7/15 versus 6/58) - its Huang 2023 Table 1 inputs are not verified by any retained original and are quarantined, which is scoped absence and not a finding that the published counts are wrong; the proposition that a zero-event arm yields no magnitude at any denominator, which is mathematically false; the size-versus-biology explanation of the death excess; the claim to cover the entire published experience or to combine literatures nobody had combined, which no systematic search supports and which prior reviews contradict; and the refutation of the 2020 review's cautious metastasis-free-survival trend, a different endpoint that a non-significant crude tally cannot refute. SOURCE LIMITS: no systematic search was run, so nothing here is a census; the response denominators rest on secondary provenance and no primary full text of either TKI report is held; the comparator arms are labelled non-TAF15 and no comparison against a trial-level verified EWSR1 arm exists anywhere in this synthesis; the reported prognostic analyses do not establish an independent partner effect IN EITHER DIRECTION, and no event count, coefficient or model specification is available to assess them; no signed direction of follow-up, selection or missingness bias is claimed; and no time-to-event quantity, hazard ratio or individual prognosis is derived. It asserts no efficacy, safety, selectivity, therapeutic window or clinical readiness for any agent, in any patient group, at any line of therapy, and no wet-lab work was performed.
 
